# Snyk policy.
#
# Every entry below silences an infrastructure rule for Terraform that is never
# applied to a cloud. The .agents and .test-deps trees hold harness fixtures:
# they are applied against a local simulator and destroyed inside the same
# test run.
#
# Hardening them would be wrong, not merely unnecessary. A bucket that lives for
# the duration of one test against a simulator does not need MFA delete,
# versioning or a customer-managed key, and adding them would stop the fixture
# resembling the minimal configuration a consumer actually writes — which is the
# only thing it is there to prove.
#
# The ignores carry no expiry because the reason cannot expire: these files are
# fixtures by construction, not infrastructure awaiting hardening. Each is
# scoped to the fixture path, so the same rule is still reported anywhere else —
# terraform/modules/ holds the real deployable infrastructure and is deliberately
# not silenced here.
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  SNYK-CC-AWS-415:
    - '.agents/shauth-provider-logout/terraform/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
    - '.test-deps/shauth/terraform/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
  SNYK-CC-AWS-421:
    - '.agents/shauth-provider-logout/terraform/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
    - '.test-deps/shauth/terraform/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
  SNYK-CC-TF-138:
    - '.agents/shauth-provider-logout/terraform/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
    - '.test-deps/shauth/terraform/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
  SNYK-CC-TF-56:
    - '.agents/shauth-provider-logout/terraform/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
    - '.agents/shauth-provider-logout/terraform/tests/fixtures/resource_derived_vpc_link/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
    - '.test-deps/shauth/terraform/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
    - '.test-deps/shauth/terraform/tests/fixtures/resource_derived_vpc_link/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
  SNYK-CC-TF-73:
    - '.agents/shauth-provider-logout/terraform/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
    - '.agents/shauth-provider-logout/terraform/tests/fixtures/resource_derived_vpc_link/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
    - '.test-deps/shauth/terraform/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.
    - '.test-deps/shauth/terraform/tests/fixtures/resource_derived_vpc_link/main.tf > *':
        reason: Simulator/harness Terraform fixture, applied only against a local simulator and destroyed in-test.

# The entries below are decisions about the deployable modules under
# terraform/modules, not fixtures: each names a hardening rule the modules
# do not follow and the reason the deployment is shaped that way. A reason
# that stops holding is the signal to remove the entry and apply the rule.
  SNYK-CC-AZURE-516:
    - 'terraform/modules/aca/main.tf > resource > azurerm_virtual_network[this] > ddos_protection_plan':
        reason: An Azure DDoS Protection plan is a per-subscription product priced in the thousands of dollars a month; the Container Apps environment's network is internal and a plan is an operator's decision, not the module's.
  SNYK-CC-AZURE-595:
    - 'terraform/modules/aca/main.tf > resource > azurerm_container_registry[this] > georeplications':
        reason: Geo-replication needs the Premium registry SKU and replicates every overlay image to a second region; the registry serves one region's workloads and the SKU is the acr_sku variable an operator sets.
    - 'terraform/modules/azf/main.tf > resource > azurerm_container_registry[main] > georeplications':
        reason: Geo-replication needs the Premium registry SKU and replicates every overlay image to a second region; the registry serves one region's workloads and the SKU is the acr_sku variable an operator sets.
  SNYK-CC-GCP-274:
    - 'terraform/modules/cloudrun/main.tf > resource > google_storage_bucket[logs] > logging':
        reason: This is the bucket every other bucket in the module writes its access logs to; a log bucket that logged to itself would loop, and one logging to a further bucket only moves the same finding there.
    - 'terraform/modules/gcf/main.tf > resource > google_storage_bucket[logs] > logging':
        reason: This is the bucket every other bucket in the module writes its access logs to; a log bucket that logged to itself would loop, and one logging to a further bucket only moves the same finding there.
  SNYK-CC-TF-45:
    - 'terraform/modules/lambda/codebuild.tf > input > resource > aws_s3_bucket[access_logs] > logging':
        reason: This is the bucket the build-context bucket writes its access logs to; a log bucket that logged to itself would loop, and one logging to a further bucket only moves the same finding there.
  SNYK-CC-AWS-427:
    - 'terraform/modules/ecs/main.tf > resource > aws_subnet[public] > map_public_ip_on_launch':
        reason: Fargate tasks in this subnet pull their images and dial the backend's callback through their own public address; private addressing needs a NAT gateway, a topology and cost decision the module leaves to the operator.
  SNYK-CC-TF-72:
    - 'terraform/modules/ecs/main.tf > resource > aws_security_group_rule[task_all_egress]':
        reason: A task's workload is the user's container, which reaches registries, package indexes and the backend's callback address; restricting its egress is a deployment policy the module cannot decide for every workload.
  SNYK-CC-TF-126:
    - 'terraform/modules/ecs/main.tf > resource > aws_ecr_repository[main] > image_tag_mutability':
        reason: The repository holds the runner image under the runner-amd64 tag, rebuilt in place on every runner build; overlay images are content-addressed tags that never change. An immutable repository would refuse the runner rebuild.
    - 'terraform/modules/lambda/main.tf > resource > aws_ecr_repository[main] > image_tag_mutability':
        reason: The repository holds the runner image under the runner-amd64 tag, rebuilt in place on every runner build; overlay images are content-addressed tags that never change. An immutable repository would refuse the runner rebuild.
  SNYK-CC-TF-127:
    - 'terraform/modules/lambda/codebuild.tf > resource > aws_s3_bucket_versioning[build_context] > *':
        reason: MFA delete can only be enabled by the account's root user with a hardware MFA device through the S3 API; Terraform run as a deployment role cannot set it, and the bucket holds one-day build contexts.
    - 'terraform/modules/lambda/codebuild.tf > resource > aws_s3_bucket_versioning[access_logs] > *':
        reason: MFA delete can only be enabled by the account's root user with a hardware MFA device through the S3 API; Terraform run as a deployment role cannot set it.
